{"id":"abc609944c1f1b77ba2ceb72e15b5021eb1c6491","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"abc609944c1f1b77ba2ceb72e15b5021eb1c6491","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/pnpr-rate-limits-and-coalescing.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": minor","+---","+","+Package write requests now check permissions before buffering large request bodies. Upstream packument fetches are coalesced across concurrent requests. Login endpoints enforce rate limits, and incoming requests support a configurable `requestTimeout` [pnpm/tasks#131](https://github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/131)."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/config_file.rs","lines":["@@ -187,6 +187,9 @@ pub(super) struct ConfigFile {","     /// Header name trusted to supply client IP addresses (`x-forwarded-for`, `forwarded`, `x-real-ip`).","     #[serde(default, rename = \"trustedProxyHeader\", alias = \"trusted_proxy_header\")]","     pub(super) trusted_proxy_header: Option<String>,","+    /// Request processing timeout (e.g. `60s`, `1m`).","+    #[serde(default, rename = \"requestTimeout\", alias = \"request_timeout\")]","+    pub(super) request_timeout: Option<Interval>,","     /// pnpr-only browser access policy. Cross-origin access stays disabled","     /// when this block is absent or its allowlist is empty.","     #[serde(default)]"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -164,6 +164,13 @@ impl std::fmt::Debug for Config {","     }"," }"," ","+#[cfg_attr(","+    dylint_lib = \"perfectionist\",","+    expect(","+        perfectionist::too_many_struct_fields,","+        reason = \"registry HTTP configuration reflects top-level server options\"","+    )","+)]"," #[derive(Debug, Clone)]"," pub struct HttpConfig {","     /// Address the HTTP server binds to.","@@ -186,6 +193,14 @@ pub struct HttpConfig {","     pub trusted_proxies: Vec<IpNetwork>,","     /// Which forwarding header to inspect when behind a trusted proxy.","     pub trusted_proxy_header: TrustedProxyHeader,","+    /// Request processing timeout. If a request handler takes longer than","+    /// this duration to process, it is aborted and returns 504 Gateway Timeout.","+    /// `None` or 0 disables request timeouts.","+    pub request_timeout: Option<Duration>,","+}","+","+impl HttpConfig {","+    pub const DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_mins(1);"," }"," "," #[derive(Debug, Clone)]"],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/loading.rs","lines":["@@ -253,6 +253,20 @@ fn build_http_config(","         Some(raw) => raw.parse::<super::TrustedProxyHeader>()?,","         None => super::TrustedProxyHeader::default(),","     };","+    let request_timeout = match file.request_timeout.as_ref() {","+        Some(interval) => {","+            let duration =","+                super::parse_interval(&interval.0)","+                    .ok_or_else(|| RegistryError::InvalidConfig {","+                        reason: format!(","+                            \"http.requestTimeout {:?} is not a valid interval\",","+                            interval.0,","+                        ),","+                    })?;","+            (!duration.is_zero()).then_some(duration)","+        }","+        None => Some(super::HttpConfig::DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT),","+    };","     Ok(super::HttpConfig {","         listen,","         public_url: public_url.unwrap_or_else(|| format!(\"http://{listen}\")),","@@ -262,6 +276,7 @@ fn build_http_config(","         packument_ttl: Config::DEFAULT_PACKUMENT_TTL,","         trusted_proxies,","         trusted_proxy_header,","+        request_timeout,","     })"," }"," "],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/presets.rs","lines":["@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@ impl Config {","                 packument_ttl: Self::DEFAULT_PACKUMENT_TTL,","                 trusted_proxies: Vec::new(),","                 trusted_proxy_header: super::TrustedProxyHeader::default(),","+                request_timeout: Some(super::HttpConfig::DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT),","             },","             storage: super::StorageConfig {","                 cache_dir: default_cache_dir(&storage),"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/config/src/tests/server_options.rs","lines":["@@ -367,3 +367,27 @@ upstreams: {}","     assert_eq!(config.http.trusted_proxies.len(), 4);","     assert_eq!(config.http.trusted_proxy_header, super::super::TrustedProxyHeader::Forwarded);"," }","+","+#[test]","+fn request_timeout_defaults_and_overrides() {","+    let base_config =","+        Config::from_yaml_str(\"storage: ./s\\n\", Path::new(\"/x\"), listen(), None).unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(base_config.http.request_timeout, Some(crate::HttpConfig::DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT));","+","+    let custom_yaml = \"storage: ./s\\nrequestTimeout: 15s\\n\";","+    let custom_config =","+        Config::from_yaml_str(custom_yaml, Path::new(\"/x\"), listen(), None).unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(custom_config.http.request_timeout, Some(std::time::Duration::from_secs(15)));","+","+    let disabled_yaml = \"storage: ./s\\nrequestTimeout: 0\\n\";","+    let disabled_config =","+        Config::from_yaml_str(disabled_yaml, Path::new(\"/x\"), listen(), None).unwrap();","+    assert_eq!(disabled_config.http.request_timeout, None);","+","+    let invalid_yaml = \"storage: ./s\\nrequestTimeout: invalid_val\\n\";","+    let err = Config::from_yaml_str(invalid_yaml, Path::new(\"/x\"), listen(), None).unwrap_err();","+    assert!(","+        matches!(err, RegistryError::InvalidConfig { ref reason } if reason.contains(\"requestTimeout\")),","+        \"expected InvalidConfig with requestTimeout, got {err:?}\",","+    );","+}"],"additions":24,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/error/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -287,6 +287,26 @@ pub enum RegistryError {","     #[from(skip)]","     TooManyUsers { max: u64 },"," ","+    /// The client sent too many requests. Maps to 429 Too Many Requests.","+    #[display(\"Too many requests: {reason}\")]","+    #[from(skip)]","+    TooManyRequests {","+        #[error(not(source))]","+        reason: String,","+    },","+","+    /// Request processing timed out. Maps to 504 Gateway Timeout.","+    #[display(\"Request timed out: {reason}\")]","+    #[from(skip)]","+    RequestTimeout {","+        #[error(not(source))]","+        reason: String,","+    },","+","+    /// An error wrapped in an `Arc` so multiple concurrent waiters sharing a","+    /// singleflight upstream fetch can clone the failure.","+    Shared(std::sync::Arc<RegistryError>),","+","     #[display(\"Internal error: {reason}\")]","     #[from(skip)]","     Internal {"],"additions":20,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/error/src/response.rs","lines":["@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ impl RegistryError {","             | RegistryError::UpstreamBody { .. }","             | RegistryError::UpstreamUnavailable { .. } => true,","             RegistryError::UpstreamStatus { status, .. } => *status >= 500,","+            RegistryError::Shared(inner) => inner.is_transient_upstream_error(),","             _ => false,","         }","     }","@@ -60,6 +61,9 @@ impl RegistryError {","             RegistryError::OsvVulnerability { .. } => \"osv_vulnerability\",","             RegistryError::RegistrationDisabled => \"registration_disabled\",","             RegistryError::TooManyUsers { .. } => \"too_many_users\",","+            RegistryError::TooManyRequests { .. } => \"too_many_requests\",","+            RegistryError::RequestTimeout { .. } => \"request_timeout\",","+            RegistryError::Shared(inner) => inner.log_kind(),","             _ => self.storage_log_kind(),","         }","     }","@@ -116,11 +120,17 @@ impl RegistryError {"," ","     #[must_use]","     pub fn log_message(&self) -> String {","+        if let RegistryError::Shared(inner) = self {","+            return inner.log_message();","+        }","         redact_url_credentials(&self.to_string())","     }"," ","     #[must_use]","     pub fn public_message(&self) -> String {","+        if let RegistryError::Shared(inner) = self {","+            return inner.public_message();","+        }","         let status = self.status_code();","         if status.is_server_error() {","             return status","@@ -178,6 +188,9 @@ impl RegistryError {","             | RegistryError::OsvVulnerability { .. }","             | RegistryError::RegistrationDisabled","             | RegistryError::TooManyUsers { .. } => StatusCode::FORBIDDEN,","+            RegistryError::TooManyRequests { .. } => StatusCode::TOO_MANY_REQUESTS,","+            RegistryError::RequestTimeout { .. } => StatusCode::GATEWAY_TIMEOUT,","+            RegistryError::Shared(inner) => inner.status_code(),","             _ => self.storage_status_code(),","         }","     }"],"additions":13,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/package-name/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ pub enum OciNameError {"," /// image repository."," /// Construction applies the ecosystem's normalization and validation before"," /// the name can be used as a storage or cache key.","-#[derive(Debug, Clone)]","+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]"," pub struct CanonicalPackageName {","     raw: String,","     /// The unscoped portion — for `@scope/name` and `namespace/image` this is"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server.rs","lines":["@@ -94,11 +94,15 @@ mod oidc_groups;"," mod package_mutation;"," mod publishing;"," mod pypi;","+mod rate_limit;","+use rate_limit::LoginRateLimiter;"," mod registry_directory;"," mod routing;"," mod rule_admin;"," mod rule_overrides;"," mod scim;","+mod singleflight;","+use singleflight::Singleflight;"," mod staged;"," mod striped_locks;"," mod team_access;","@@ -206,8 +210,8 @@ mod state;"," use state::AppInner;"," "," #[derive(Clone)]","-struct AppState {","-    inner: Arc<AppInner>,","+pub(super) struct AppState {","+    pub(super) inner: Arc<AppInner>,"," }"," "," #[derive(serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]"],"additions":6,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/package_mutation.rs","lines":["@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ async fn rewrite_packument("," "," /// A packument rewrite adds nothing but may remove anything, so it is held to"," /// both write permissions.","-fn authorize_rewrite(","+pub(super) fn authorize_rewrite(","     state: &AppState,","     identity: &Identity,","     source: &RegistrySource,"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/rate_limit.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,157 @@","+use std::{","+    collections::HashMap,","+    net::IpAddr,","+    sync::Mutex,","+    time::{Duration, Instant},","+};","+","+#[cfg(test)]","+mod tests;","+","+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]","+enum RateLimitKey {","+    Ip(IpAddr),","+    IpUser(IpAddr, String),","+    User(String),","+}","+","+struct AttemptRecord {","+    count: u32,","+    first_attempt: Instant,","+}","+","+struct RateLimiterInner {","+    map: HashMap<RateLimitKey, AttemptRecord>,","+    last_eviction: Instant,","+}","+","+/// Tracks failed login attempts to protect against password brute-forcing","+/// and CPU exhaustion from repetitive bcrypt calls.","+pub(crate) struct LoginRateLimiter {","+    window: Duration,","+    max_ip_user_attempts: u32,","+    max_ip_attempts: u32,","+    max_user_attempts: u32,","+    records: Mutex<RateLimiterInner>,","+}","+","+impl Default for LoginRateLimiter {","+    fn default() -> Self {","+        Self::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 5, 20, 5)","+    }","+}","+","+impl LoginRateLimiter {","+    pub(crate) fn new(","+        window: Duration,","+        max_ip_user_attempts: u32,","+        max_ip_attempts: u32,","+        max_user_attempts: u32,","+    ) -> Self {","+        Self {","+            window,","+            max_ip_user_attempts,","+            max_ip_attempts,","+            max_user_attempts,","+            records: Mutex::new(RateLimiterInner {","+                map: HashMap::new(),","+                last_eviction: Instant::now(),","+            }),","+        }","+    }","+","+    fn check_key(","+        &self,","+        map: &HashMap<RateLimitKey, AttemptRecord>,","+        key: &RateLimitKey,","+        max_attempts: u32,","+        now: Instant,","+    ) -> Result<(), u64> {","+        if let Some(record) = map.get(key)","+            && record.count >= max_attempts","+        {","+            let elapsed = now.duration_since(record.first_attempt);","+            if elapsed < self.window {","+                let retry_after = self.window","+                    .saturating_sub(elapsed)","+                    .as_secs()","+                    .max(1);","+                return Err(retry_after);","+            }","+        }","+        Ok(())","+    }","+","+    /// Check if a login attempt from `client_ip` for `username` is currently throttled.","+    /// Returns `Err(retry_after_seconds)` if rate limited.","+    pub(crate) fn check(&self, client_ip: Option<IpAddr>, username: &str) -> Result<(), u64> {","+        let now = Instant::now();","+        let mut inner = self.records.lock().unwrap();","+","+        // Evict expired entries periodically or when map exceeds size threshold","+        if now.duration_since(inner.last_eviction) >= Duration::from_secs(30)","+            || inner.map.len() > 1024","+        {","+            inner.map.retain(|_, record| now.duration_since(record.first_attempt) < self.window);","+            inner.last_eviction = now;","+        }","+","+        if let Some(ip_address) = client_ip {","+            self.check_key(","+                &inner.map,","+                &RateLimitKey::IpUser(ip_address, username.to_string()),","+                self.max_ip_user_attempts,","+                now,","+            )?;","+            self.check_key(&inner.map, &RateLimitKey::Ip(ip_address), self.max_ip_attempts, now)?;","+        } else {","+            self.check_key(","+                &inner.map,","+                &RateLimitKey::User(username.to_string()),","+                self.max_user_attempts,","+                now,","+            )?;","+        }","+","+        Ok(())","+    }","+","+    /// Record a failed login attempt for `client_ip` and `username`.","+    pub(crate) fn record_failure(&self, client_ip: Option<IpAddr>, username: &str) {","+        let now = Instant::now();","+        let mut inner = self.records.lock().unwrap();","+","+        let keys = if let Some(ip_address) = client_ip {","+            vec![","+                RateLimitKey::IpUser(ip_address, username.to_string()),","+                RateLimitKey::Ip(ip_address),","+            ]","+        } else {","+            vec![RateLimitKey::User(username.to_string())]","+        };","+","+        for key in keys {","+            inner.map","+                .entry(key)","+                .and_modify(|record| {","+                    if now.duration_since(record.first_attempt) >= self.window {","+                        record.count = 1;","+                        record.first_attempt = now;","+                    } else {","+                        record.count += 1;","+                    }","+                })","+                .or_insert(AttemptRecord { count: 1, first_attempt: now });","+        }","+    }","+","+    /// Clear failure count for `(client_ip, username)` or `username` on successful authentication.","+    pub(crate) fn record_success(&self, client_ip: Option<IpAddr>, username: &str) {","+        let mut inner = self.records.lock().unwrap();","+        if let Some(ip_address) = client_ip {","+            inner.map.remove(&RateLimitKey::IpUser(ip_address, username.to_string()));","+        } else {","+            inner.map.remove(&RateLimitKey::User(username.to_string()));","+        }","+    }","+}"],"additions":157,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/rate_limit/tests.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@","+use std::{","+    net::{IpAddr, Ipv4Addr},","+    time::Duration,","+};","+","+use super::LoginRateLimiter;","+","+#[test]","+fn rate_limiter_allows_attempts_under_threshold() {","+    let limiter = LoginRateLimiter::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 3, 10, 5);","+    let ip_address = IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::new(192, 168, 1, 10));","+","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn rate_limiter_throttles_user_after_exceeding_threshold() {","+    let limiter = LoginRateLimiter::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 3, 10, 5);","+    let ip_address = IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::new(192, 168, 1, 10));","+","+    for _ in 0..3 {","+        assert!(","+            limiter","+                .check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\")","+                .is_ok(),","+        );","+        limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    }","+","+    let check_result = limiter.check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    assert!(check_result.is_err(), \"expected throttling after 3 failures\");","+","+    // Failures from IP A must not block the same username from IP B","+    let other_ip = IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::new(192, 168, 1, 20));","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(other_ip), \"alice\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+","+    // Other user from same IP should still be allowed if under IP threshold","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(ip_address), \"bob\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn rate_limiter_throttles_ip_after_exceeding_ip_threshold() {","+    let limiter = LoginRateLimiter::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 5, 4, 10);","+    let ip_address = IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::new(10, 0, 0, 1));","+","+    for user_index in 0..4 {","+        let username = format!(\"user_{user_index}\");","+        assert!(","+            limiter","+                .check(Some(ip_address), &username)","+                .is_ok(),","+        );","+        limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), &username);","+    }","+","+    // Now IP limit of 4 is reached","+    let check_result = limiter.check(Some(ip_address), \"another_user\");","+    assert!(check_result.is_err(), \"expected IP throttling after 4 failures across users\");","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn rate_limiter_resets_on_success() {","+    let limiter = LoginRateLimiter::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 3, 10, 5);","+    let ip_address = IpAddr::V4(Ipv4Addr::new(192, 168, 1, 10));","+","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    limiter.record_success(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+","+    // After success, previous failure count for alice is cleared","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    limiter.record_failure(Some(ip_address), \"alice\");","+    assert!(","+        limiter","+            .check(Some(ip_address), \"alice\")","+            .is_ok(),","+    );","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn rate_limiter_throttles_by_username_even_when_ip_is_none() {","+    let limiter = LoginRateLimiter::new(Duration::from_mins(1), 5, 10, 2);","+    assert!(limiter.check(None, \"alice\").is_ok());","+    limiter.record_failure(None, \"alice\");","+    assert!(limiter.check(None, \"alice\").is_ok());","+    limiter.record_failure(None, \"alice\");","+    assert!(limiter.check(None, \"alice\").is_err(), \"expected throttling by username\");","+}"],"additions":112,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpr/crates/pnpr/src/server/routing.rs","lines":["@@ -21,9 +21,9 @@ use std::sync::Arc;"," use axum::{","     Router,","     extract::{DefaultBodyLimit, Path, RawQuery, State},","-    http::{HeaderMap, HeaderValue, Method, header},","+    http::{HeaderMap, HeaderValue, Method, StatusCode, header},","     middleware,","-    response::Response,","+    response::{IntoResponse, Response},","     routing::{any, delete, get, post, put},"," };"," use tower_http::cors::{AllowOrigin, CorsLayer};","@@ -34,21 +34,21 @@ use pnpr_registry::Ecosystem;"," use serde::Deserialize;"," "," use super::{","-    AppInner, AppState, AuthedCaller, MAX_ARTIFACT_BLOB_BODY_BYTES,","+    Action, AppInner, AppState, AuthedCaller, CanonicalPackageName, MAX_ARTIFACT_BLOB_BODY_BYTES,","     MAX_ARTIFACT_PUBLISH_BODY_BYTES, MAX_ARTIFACT_RESOLVE_BODY_BYTES, MAX_LOGIN_BODY_BYTES,","-    MAX_PIPELINE_RUN_BODY_BYTES, MAX_PUBLISH_BODY_BYTES, MAX_TEAM_BODY_BYTES, TargetRegistry,","-    addressed_registry, authenticate, batch, caller_scoped, cargo, compiler_cache, delete_package,","-    delete_session_token, delete_tarball, delete_token_by_key, get_dist_tags, get_org_teams,","-    get_profile, get_team_members, get_token_list, get_whoami,","+    MAX_PIPELINE_RUN_BODY_BYTES, MAX_PUBLISH_BODY_BYTES, MAX_TEAM_BODY_BYTES, RegistrySource,","+    TargetRegistry, addressed_registry, authenticate, authorize, batch, caller_scoped, cargo,","+    compiler_cache, delete_package, delete_session_token, delete_tarball, delete_token_by_key,","+    get_dist_tags, get_org_teams, get_profile, get_team_members, get_token_list, get_whoami,","     health::{serve_live, serve_ping, serve_ready},","-    not_found, oci, pnpr_protocols_disabled, private_no_cache, publish_package, put_login, pypi,","-    remove_dist_tag, require_artifact_caller, require_pipeline_caller, require_resolver_caller,","-    serve_artifact_blob, serve_artifact_blob_size, serve_batch_publish, serve_get_pipeline_run,","-    serv